From 1fc3dac0a671c2c215d986765ebb1f50810f017d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 18:24:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] Clone a search to another country, filter on market
 position, and a dashboard that explains itself
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three things, one theme: the person at the keyboard should not need the
docs.

Clone. Vinted lets a buyer shop across its EU sites, its filter ids are the
same on every site, and .de or .pl carry many times the listings of .sk —
yet every search here ran on one domain. The Edit form now offers "Also
watch this on vinted.xx": the same URL with a new domain, same filters,
same destinations. A listing shown on several sites is alerted once, since
the item id is the key.

Market filter. "Only the cheapest N%" compares a new listing with
everything the search has seen in thirty days (the market table from the
previous change) and lets it through only if it sits in that share. Unlike a
fixed price cap it follows the season by itself. Nobody is asked to know
what a percentile is: the field says "only the cheapest … %", the tooltip
explains it in a sentence, and the alert states the result in words —
"cheaper than 88% of 312 similar listings seen this month" — which is also
stored per listing and sent to the agent. Inactive below ten price points.

Dashboard. Every field and column has a ? tooltip in plain language; the
searches table has a legend for its states; an explainer under the add
form says how the filters combine; a Help page carries a glossary, what
each part of an alert means, and the running settings; every action ends in
a success notice; delete asks first and says what pausing would keep
instead; icons are SVG, the nav marks the current page, focus rings show
for keyboard users, reduced motion is honoured, and the dark theme no
longer contains hard-coded light colours. Migration 0011.
